[132.593508, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[132.628925, "o", "One Converse call from us-east-1 (the source Region) with modelId global.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\r\n\r\nThe checks IAM makes (AWS's cross-Region inference pages), and where each one points:\r\n  1. the profile Region us-east-1    arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1:111122223333:inference-profile/global.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\r\n  2. the model   Region us-east-1    arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1::foundation-model/anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\r\n                                    with bedrock:InferenceProfileArn set\r\n  3. the model   Region unspecified  arn:aws:bedrock:::foundation-model/anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\r\n                                    with bedrock:InferenceProfileArn set\r\n\r\nWhere the prompt may be processed: us-east-1, unspecified\r\n  'unspecified' = the Region-less model ARN: AWS says any supported commercial Region worldwide.\r\nAnyCompany's rule: Helpdesk prompts and answers may only be processed in US Regions.\r\nVerdict: BREAKS the rule\r\n"]
